<p><a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Fumble_boots" title="Fumble boots">Fumble boots</a> and <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Levitation_boots" title="Levitation boots">levitation boots</a> are both 30zm, but are of different <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Weight" title="Weight">weights</a>. They are often <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Cursed" class="mw-redirect" title="Cursed">cursed</a>.
</p><p><a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Speed_boots" title="Speed boots">Speed boots</a>, <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Jumping_boots" title="Jumping boots">jumping boots</a>, and <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Water_walking_boots" title="Water walking boots">water walking boots</a> are all priced at 50zm. They are easily identified once worn: speed boots auto-identify if you are not already very fast (<a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Potion_of_speed" title="Potion of speed">potion of speed</a> or <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Spellbook_of_haste_self" title="Spellbook of haste self">haste self</a> spell), jumping boots allow you to <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Jump" class="mw-redirect" title="Jump">jump</a>, and boots of water walking are otherwise mundane.
</p><p><a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Elven_boots" title="Elven boots">Elven boots</a> cause you to "walk very quietly" and self-identify if you are not already <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Stealth" title="Stealth">stealthy</a>. <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Kicking_boots" title="Kicking boots">Kicking boots</a> are made of metal, and consequently add to <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Spell" title="Spell">spell</a> failure percentage.
</p>
