<p>The cloaks of displacement and protection both cost 50zm, and are the only ones at that price with a randomized appearance. If a cloak costs 60zm and has a randomized appearance, then it is either invisibility, magic resistance, or a +1 cloak of the first two types.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Other_armor">Other armor</span></h4>
<p>All magical <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Randomized_appearance" title="Randomized appearance">randomized</a> <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Helm" title="Helm">helms</a> (<a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Helm_of_brilliance" title="Helm of brilliance">brilliance</a>, <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Helm_of_opposite_alignment" title="Helm of opposite alignment">opposite alignment</a>, and <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Helm_of_telepathy" title="Helm of telepathy">telepathy</a>) cost 50zm; the <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Helmet" title="Helmet">helmet</a> costs 10zm.
</p><p>All magical <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Gloves" title="Gloves">gloves</a> (<a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Gauntlets_of_dexterity" title="Gauntlets of dexterity">dexterity</a>, <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Gauntlets_of_fumbling" title="Gauntlets of fumbling">fumbling</a>, and <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Gauntlets_of_power" title="Gauntlets of power">power</a>) cost 50zm; <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Leather_gloves" title="Leather gloves">leather gloves</a> cost 8zm.
</p><p>Positive <a href="https://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Enchantment" title="Enchantment">enchantment</a> on a piece of armor increases the base price by 10zm per point of enchantment. In theory, a +2 or better pair of fumble boots might be confused for one of the much more useful 50zm boots, but the probability for positive enchantments on harmful items is too low to be worth worrying about.
</p>
